{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Mercury Retrograde", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Writing a Persuasive Paragraph", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 17, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Exchange information about hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Writing Tips: <span class=\"italic\">That</span>-Clauses: Reporting Verbs to Express Opinions and Beliefs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In writing, you often want to sound more formal than you would in natural conversation.<br/> There are some tips to make your writing more formal.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use <span class=\"italic\">that</span>-clauses after some reporting verbs, you can structure it differently to make it sound more formal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">felt that the results </span>were satisfactory.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">felt the results to be </span>satisfactory.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here the structure is: object + infinitive ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Other verbs you can use in this way are: <span class=\"italic\">acknowledge, assume, believe, consider, declare, expect, find, presume, report, think, understand.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you use a <span class=\"italic\">that</span>-clause after an active form of some verbs, you must include an object between the verb and the <span class=\"italic\">that</span>-clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">notified the bank that </span>I had changed my phone number.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Other verbs you use in this way are:<span class=\"italic\"> assure, convince, inform, persuade, reassure, remind, tell.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I told you that Mercury retrograde was at the heart of my problems!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Non-believers may think that their connection is coincidental and astronomy to be nonsensical.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We all know that earth and the rest of the solar system hold a mysterious past and that there are elements of our existence that cannot be fully explained.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Similarly, it is advised that people hold off on making important decisions during this unstable period.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "And for the 55-69% of Americans who don't think that astrology is credible, just remember: the planet Mercury will continue to exert its influence, whether you believe it or not.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I firmly believe that Mercury retrograde is the culprit.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "plausible", "type": "name"}, {"content": "possibly true; believable or realistic", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On the other hand, skeptics of this phenomenon are unable to provide a plausible alternative explanation. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use in a persuasive paragraph about a controversial topic.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to act up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be acting incorrectly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did your hard drive start acting up within the last couple weeks? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "culprit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone or something that has one something wrong", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Mercury's retrograde, a phenomenon that occurs about three times a year, is the obvious culprit. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nonsensical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very foolish or silly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Non-believers may think that their connection is coincidental and astrology to be nonsensical. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "correlation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the relationship between things that happen or change together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This event, which entails the planet appearing to move backward in its orbit, has a direct correlation with all things related to timing and traffic, transportation and communication.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "awry", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not working correctly or happening in the expected way ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Therefore, as Mercury rules any shift or change in direction can lead to things on Earth going awry. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a 150-180 word persuasive paragraph about a strange event or coincidence.  For example: the belief in aliens, mermaids, robots taking over the world.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include both your own and the opposing point of view.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use linking words to connect ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include the phrases - <i>I firmly believe ...</i> and <i>We all know ...</i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When completed, read the paragraph aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a persuasive paragraph about strange events or coincidences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I include my own and the opposing point of view in persuasive paragraphs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use linking words to connect ideas.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can write a persuasive paragraph.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can write about coincidences and strange events.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can write about opinions and beliefs. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you believe in astrology? What star sign are you?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Are you a persuasive person? Can you make people change their minds about topics or issue? How?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Writing Spot: Mercury's retrograde - Can I make you a believer?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text